cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying data, please cite this version and the associated preprint (arXiv:2608.06968)."
title: "How a shared state is described determines whether AI agents synchronize: data and code"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic circular-agent engine, observation-map encoders, acquisition
  runners, statistical analyses and figure code for the study of how the
  encoding of a physical state into model input changes both the microscopic
  response operator of a language-model agent and the collective outcome of a
  population of such agents.
type: software
